From fb3aeb69801cfb88ce34588eff852949e3c8978a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@users.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:56:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Shaders + VPVulkan: multisampled texture reads,
 OpImageQuerySamples, vkCmdResolveImage

VPIR: Resource::multisampled (2d / 2d_array sampled textures), image operand "sample" (u32 sample
index, required on image_fetch of a multisampled texture), op image_samples (u32; 1 for other
textures). Verifier, text form and optimizer know them. MSL: texture2d_ms / texture2d_ms_array /
depth2d_ms(_array), .read(coord, [layer,] sample), get_num_samples().
SPIR-V lowering: images with MS=1 become multisampled resources; OpImageFetch's Sample operand
(texelFetch of sampler2DMS, subpassLoad of MS inputs) is honoured, sample 0 when absent;
OpImageQuerySamples returns the real count (was always 1).
vkCmdResolveImage: an empty pass over the source (load) whose StoreAndResolve resolves into the
destination, colour or depth (was dropped). Metal resolves whole attachments: partial regions are
resolved whole (logged).

Tests: vpmsl.golden.ms_textures (new golden), gpu_vulkan.depth_resolve (vkCmdResolveImage).

